  "query_preview": "..A broad ridge over the area today will give way to a\nweak shortwave trough that is currently rippling through the \nPacNW and western Nevada. Some high clouds will continue to cross\nUtah ahead of it, otherwise little moisture will be available as\nthis trough crosses Utah Tuesday morning. Main impact will be some\ncold advection on Tuesday under a northwesterly flow. While \ntemperatures in the valleys will cool slightly, stronger cooling \naloft should weaken the inversions in place, clearing out some of \nthe valley haze. After the trough exits the area, a strong ridge \nwill return to the area Tuesday night through late week.\n\nGlobal deterministic models are in fairly good agreement bringing\nthe next trough into the area for Saturday. This progressive \nsystem would bring a quick shot of widespread valley rain and \nmountain snow to the area. However, cluster analysis of global\nensembles show a 50/50 split between this wet solution and a drier\nsolution where the trough remains well offshore.",
